# Z3 forgets a timeout that fires inside one of its nested resource scopes,
# which a budget of a millisecond or two makes likely: such a check ran
# without end. A check is interrupted again until it returns, so every query
# ends and the function gets a verdict (which one depends on timing).
#
# RUN: %python -c "import subprocess, sys; sys.exit(subprocess.run(sys.argv[1:], timeout=120).returncode not in (0, 1))" \
# RUN:   %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --int-encoding=bitvector --timeout=1 \
# RUN:   %S/Inputs/tiny_timeout.cpp -- > %t.out 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.out

# CHECK: {{Verified|Unresolved}}: copy
